+# Review: retry on gateway timeout
+
+Retrying a timed-out payment is reasonable, but `payments.charge` is not safe to retry as called.
+
+- `charge`'s docstring says it is NOT idempotent unless a `key` is passed, and that a call which timed out may still have gone through. `checkout.pay` retries without a key, so a timeout after the gateway accepted the charge makes the customer pay twice (up to three times).
+- Fix: pass `key=order["id"]` on every attempt, so a retry returns the first receipt.
+- No test simulates a timeout after success.
+
+VERDICT: request changes
